# Cubric Vision — curated Python dependency INPUT for ComfyUI custom nodes (MPI-413).
#
# This is the set WE chose. It replaces asking each custom node to resolve its own
# requirements.txt on the user's machine — 13 separate pip resolves that re-derived the
# same shared graph, installed 4 packages only to uninstall and replace them, and let
# whichever node ran last decide the version of every shared library.
#
# THIS FILE IS HAND-CURATED. The lock next to it is not:
#
#   dev_configs/python_deps.in   <- this file, edited by a human, reviewed in the diff
#   dev_configs/python_deps.txt  <- GENERATED, do not hand-edit
#
# Regenerate + drift-check:
#   node scripts/compile-node-deps.mjs --check   # is every node requirement covered here?
#   node scripts/compile-node-deps.mjs           # rewrite python_deps.txt
#
# ADDING OR BUMPING A NODE WITH REQUIREMENTS: run --check, add anything it reports to
# this file, regenerate, review the diff, commit both files. See
# docs/playbooks/add-model/ and .claude/rules/comfy_engine.md.
#
# ── What is deliberately NOT here ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# torch / torchvision / torchaudio — engine-owned, never ours to move. The local
#   engine installs them via comfy-cli's vendor branch (or the pinned macOS trio in
#   routes/engine.js step 2b, or the Windows portable archive); the Pod image pins the
#   cu130 trio and enforces it with PIP_CONSTRAINT. The compile excludes them with
#   --no-emit-package so this file can never move a user's torch.
#
# git+https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam2 — declared by ComfyUI-Impact-Pack.
#   Dropped on every platform since MPI-387: pip shells out to `git clone` for it, no
#   portable engine ships git, and it failed 100% of clean installs. It backs Impact-Pack
#   sampling nodes we never exercise; we ship SAM 1 (`sam-vit-b`) as the Impact segment
#   refiner (MPI-380).
#
# cupy / cupy-wheel — declared by ComfyUI-Frame-Interpolation's install.py. Dropped.
#   Measured 2026-08-04: cupy is ABSENT from the live engine, taichi too, and the node
#   loads fine — it is reachable only through vfi_models/ops, which none of the eagerly
#   imported model __init__ files touch. We ship exactly one FI node, `RIFE VFI`
#   (comfy_workflows/video_interpolate.json), and RIFE never uses ops. `cupy-wheel` in
#   particular is a 2.9 kB source shim whose setup.py imports pkg_resources, which modern
#   setuptools no longer ships — so it fails to build on EVERY platform on EVERY fresh
#   install, silently (MPI-413 Evidence C). Its only job is runtime CUDA detection, which
#   is exactly what this file replaces.

# ── Pinned shared set ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These were `pipPins` in js/data/modelConstants/nodesDeps.js — a per-node, hand-
# maintained repair applied AFTER each node's requirements had already drifted the
# engine. Here they are simply the requirement, so nothing drifts in the first place.
# Versions are the live proven-good set (MPI-222), unchanged.
numpy==2.5.1
scipy==1.18.0
scikit-image==0.26.0
matplotlib==3.11.0
pillow==12.3.0
kornia==0.8.2
einops==0.8.2
transformers[timm]==5.13.0
ultralytics==8.4.78
dill==0.4.1
color-matcher==0.6.0
mss==10.2.0

# opencv — ONE variant, deliberately.
# Three nodes declared three different distributions that all install into the same
# `cv2` namespace: opencv-python (comfyui_controlnet_aux, RES4LYF),
# opencv-python-headless (Impact-Pack, Impact-Subpack, kjnodes) and
# opencv-contrib-python (Frame-Interpolation). pipPins forced TWO of them at once, so
# which cv2 an engine ended up with was last-writer-wins. The contrib+headless build is
# a superset of all three and is the right choice for a non-GUI engine.
opencv-contrib-python-headless==5.0.0.93

# ── The rest ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unpinned here on purpose: python_deps.txt pins them transitively, so the engine still
# gets one chosen set, and a node bump can move them without a hand edit.
addict
albumentations
conformer
diffusers
filelock
ftfy
fvcore
huggingface_hub>=0.25.2
librosa
# imageio-ffmpeg — NOT a transitive, and NOT the same package as `imageio` (which the
# lock already pins and which bundles no binary). It ships the ffmpeg executable, and
# OUR MpiSaveVideo hard-requires one: help_funcs.py find_ffmpeg() tries
# VHS_FORCE_FFMPEG_PATH, then this import, then shutil.which("ffmpeg"). The Windows
# portable engine satisfies none of the other two, so without this line every video op
# on every model fails at the last node, after the full sample (MPI-472, live 2026-08-07).
# It was only ever declared by comfyui-videohelpersuite's requirements.txt, which nothing
# installs since MPI-413 — and --check could not see it, because VHS is
# `installRequirements: false`. The gate now reads every locked node, not just those.
# The Pod is immune by accident: its image apt-installs ffmpeg, so which() finds one.
imageio-ffmpeg
importlib_metadata
mediapipe>=0.8.0
ninja~=1.11.1.4
omegaconf
piexif
python-dateutil
pywavelets
pyyaml
# resemble-perth — NOT declared by any node, and REQUIRED anyway. ComfyUI_Fill-ChatterBox
# ships it COMMENTED OUT of its requirements.txt, and tts.py / vc.py / mtl_tts.py each do
# `try: import perth / except: PERTH_AVAILABLE = False`, print one warning line, and then
# generate UNMARKED audio for ever. EU AI Act Art. 50 has been in force since 2026-08-02
# and Vision is the provider of the synthetic audio, so the marking is not optional and
# the failure mode is silent — which is exactly why it is pinned HERE rather than left to
# the node. Removing this line does not break a build; it ships unmarked audio (MPI-607).
resemble-perth
resampy
s3tokenizer
safetensors
scikit-learn
segment-anything
soundfile
tqdm
trimesh[easy]
yacs
yapf

# ── Platform-variant ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# onnxruntime-gpu has never published a macOS wheel, for any arch, at any version, so
# an unmarked line makes pip exit 1 and fail the WHOLE install — a Mac user could never
# get past first install of any depth model (MPI-370). Marker instead of a per-platform
# file. NOT swapped for CPU `onnxruntime`: DepthAnythingV2 runs through AIO_Preprocessor,
# which is torch-based. Add it if an ONNX-dependent preprocessor is ever wired.
onnxruntime-gpu; platform_system != "Darwin"
